## [:< ##

# name  = user-edit.form.multiline_field_names
# descr = which scalar record fields edit as windowed multi-line rows
# param = -none-

## the single list, alongside users.record.optional_fields' own vocabulary --
## see user-edit-multiline-note.yaml.  TWO call sites need this, both inside
## user-edit's own process so ONE shared module is correct here [ unlike
## users.record.sorted_fields, which user-edit duplicates BY HAND because that
## list lives in a different zenka's %code entirely ] :
## user-edit.form.schema_from_record [ a field already present on a loaded
## record ] and user-edit.form.add_field [ a field being added for the FIRST
## time via the add-a-field cycler ].
##
## MISSING FROM add_field WAS THE ACTUAL BUG, found live : schema_from_record
## alone made a freshly-added 'address' render single-line with no way to
## expand it until the form was saved and reopened, because add_field builds
## its OWN field def from the wire vocabulary's 'list'/'line' shape and had no
## way to know 'address' was one of the multiline ones -- a second independent
## name list would have drifted exactly as this file's header warns against
## generally. same lesson users.record.sorted_fields already documents for a
## different flag : a POLICY name list needs every entry point that can
## ORIGINATE a field def to read it, not just the one that happened to be
## built first.
##
## EXTEND HERE alongside users.record.optional_fields -- adding a new
## multiline field costs one line there and one word here.

return qw| address note |;

